{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RLSA-2026:100662","published":"2026-11-21T06:05:18.552458Z","modified":"2026-11-21T06:30:04.029707806Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-45861","CVE-2026-45970","CVE-2026-53049","CVE-2026-64549","CVE-2026-68148","CVE-2026-74480","CVE-2026-74493","CVE-2026-74631","CVE-2026-74637","CVE-2026-89638","CVE-2026-90347","CVE-2026-97528","CVE-2026-98232"],"summary":"Important: kernel security, bug fix, and enhancement update","details":"The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: bonding: alb: fix UAF in rlb_arp_recv during bond up/down (CVE-2026-45970)\n\n* kernel: gfs2: Fix slab-use-after-free in qd_put (CVE-2026-45861)\n\n* kernel: gfs2: add some missing log locking (CVE-2026-53049)\n\n* kernel: Bluetooth: bpa10x: avoid OOB read of revision string in bpa10x_setup() (CVE-2026-64549)\n\n* kernel: fscrypt: Add missing superblock check in find_or_insert_direct_key() (CVE-2026-68148)\n\n* kernel: net: bridge: stop fast-leave after deleting a port group (CVE-2026-74480)\n\n* kernel: net/smc: fix socket use-after-free during link group termination (CVE-2026-74493)\n\n* kernel: net: smc: fix splice entry lifetime imbalance in smc_rx_splice (CVE-2026-74631)\n\n* kernel: perf/core: Fix group leader use-after-free after sibling detach (CVE-2026-74637)\n\n* kernel: smb: client: clear setuid/setgid bit on write with cifsacl/modefromsid/posix extensions (CVE-2026-89638)\n\n* kernel: arm64: ptrace: Keep 'orig_x0' in-sync with x0 on syscall entry (CVE-2026-90347)\n\n* kernel: scsi: qla2xxx: Unlink NVMe unsol ctx before freeing on LS reject error (CVE-2026-97528)\n\n* kernel: kernel: arbitrary code execution via out-of-bounds stack access in scsi_cdl_enable() (CVE-2026-98232)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* netfilter: cve backports for 9.9 (JIRA:Rocky Linux-252129)\n\n* Backport the printk SMP startup fix [rhel-9.9.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-290042)\n\n* [IBM 9.10 FEAT] Switch SIGP to always use external call instead of emergency signal [rhel-9.9.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-303481)\n\n* Critical Bug Fixes for customer issues with lpfc [rhel-9.9.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-286163)\n\n* The Kernel panic occurred at strlen+0x0 because a race event filter treats the user space pointer as a normal pointer [rhel-9.9.z] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-291142)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"kernel","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:9","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/kernel?distro=rocky-linux-9&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:5.14.0-741.24.1.el9_9"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"BaseOS"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:100662.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-core","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:9","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/kernel-core?distro=rocky-linux-9&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:5.14.0-741.24.1.el9_9"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"BaseOS"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:100662.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-debug","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:9","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/kernel-debug?distro=rocky-linux-9&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:5.14.0-741.24.1.el9_9"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"BaseOS"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:100662.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-debug-core","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:9","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/kernel-debug-core?distro=rocky-linux-9&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:5.14.0-741.24.1.el9_9"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"BaseOS"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"http